compendia3 -- the key M ruled, and the state after the repairs
==============================================================================

1  THE KEY, AS RULED: (species, series, n-range)
   duplicated on (species, series)            9   <- compendia2.py's figure
   duplicated on (species, series, n-range)   2   <- M's key
   so the shorter key could not separate      7 distinct rows
      Si I       nd (3/2,3/2)* J=1        20–50      L811, L839
      Si I       nd (3/2,5/2)* J=3        20–56      L812, L841
   Both remaining pairs agree in EVERY printed cell but the bracket and the
   fourth decimal of delta.  Nothing printed separates them.

2  THE ONE THAT WAS NEVER A DUPLICATE, READ FROM THE VOLUME'S OWN RULE
   Ba III | nd 2[3/2]* J=2
   limits printed              289,100.000 and 306,650.000
   apart                       17,550 cm-1
   the volume's rule: one series per parent, converging on different limits.
   Two parents, two series -- and the label omits the parent.

3  AND THE LABEL FAULT IS WIDER THAN THAT ROW
   rows whose series label names its parent   14
   rows whose label does not                  582
   species that use BOTH conventions          ['Ar II', 'Ba III']
   Recorded, not repaired: which convention the volume prints is M's.

4  THE RULING 46 MATERIAL, AFTER THE PASS
   volume  scripts    files   stamps
   MC            0        0        0
   PC            0        0        1
   IoI           0        0        0
   SC            0        0        0
   the one stamp match left is W-284's recorded refusal -- "Prior counts,
   generated on a rule this volume did not print" is prose about how earlier
   counts were produced, and register 1739 turns on it.
   compendia.py pinned 23 script sites over 18 distinct scripts and 7 stamps;
   the pass of BUILD279 and BUILD281 removed them.  Figure image paths are
   excluded here, as W-286 refuses them: removing one removes a figure.
